/*****************************************************************************
    jitJ3 -- RUNG 3 OF THE jitLadder. 2026-07-31.   J2 + while.

    THE HONEST RETEST. `testWhilE` has died at 134 (SIGABRT, "Both operands to
    ICmp instruction are not of the same type") since 2026-07-30, and the
    recorded cause -- jitEmitCompare clobbering the target's stored SSA value --
    was INFERRED and later WEAKENED when the IR showed re-seeding. This rung
    settles it on clean ground rather than by argument.

    WHY THE ABORT SHOULD NOT RECUR, stated so the run can refute it: aCTionWhilE
    had NO jitting gate, so under jitting the loop EXECUTED at emit time and
    walked its condition REPEATEDLY -- re-emitting a compare against a node whose
    jitData already held the previous i1. With a gate the condition is emitted
    exactly ONCE, into the `cond` block, and the loop runs at RUN time.

    Body is a single statement on purpose: J3 adds ONE construct (`while`), and
    a multi-statement body is J5's operand-reuse question.

        while jcIn > 0;  jcIn = jcIn - 2;

        fire 1   jcIn = 10  ->  0    (5 iterations)
        fire 2   jcIn = 7   -> -1    (4 iterations, NO RECOMPILE)

    TRIP-COUNT-DEPENDENT BY CONSTRUCTION: the two inputs land on DIFFERENT
    values, so the answer proves the loop ran the right number of times. If it
    never ran: 10 and 7 unchanged. If it ran once: 8 and 5.

    SENTINEL AT THE FOOT (standing harness rule H2).
*****************************************************************************/
Start();
include(unitTests);
include(generate);
include(utilities);

search reset stack Grokking;
search Generating UnitTests bcOPs Utilities list;

register(JitLadder3);
define
    jcIn;
    jitJ3 code={
        while jcIn > 0;
            jcIn = jcIn - 2;
        };
    ;

/*  THE ORACLE'S TESTIMONY, captured while the interpreter can still give it.
    Same action, same input, interpreted -- recorded beside the asserted value.  */
jcIn = 10;
print "J3 fire 1 setup : jcIn =" jcIn:;
testing(jitJ3);
print "J3 fire 1 result: jcIn =" jcIn " (want 0)":;

jcIn = 7;
print "J3 fire 2 setup : jcIn =" jcIn " (recompile: NONE)":;
jitRefire();
print "J3 fire 2 result: jcIn =" jcIn " (want -1; 7 = loop never ran; 5 = ran once)":;

/*  ⚠ THE ORACLE IS CAPTURED LAST, AND THAT ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING -- see the
    header note. Calling the action interpreted BEFORE testing() consumes its
    isCoded state, and testing() then silently routes to jitRunIfTest (the
    hand-built smoke scaffold) instead of jitRunAction. Measured 2026-07-31.  */
jcIn = 10;
jitJ3();
print "J3 interpreted  : jcIn =" jcIn " (the oracle, input 10 -- want 0)":;

print "J3 SENTINEL -- run reached the end":;
stop();
